# Initial Setup's Optical Flow page, ported from GCSViews/ConfigurationView/ConfigHWOptFlow.cs.
#
# The claim: Activate shows the new-style page on firmware without FLOW_ENABLE - "Enable" hidden,
# the type, yaw, scale and position controls bound - and hides the height override on anything
# but a rover (ConfigHWOptFlow.cs:17-75); the type combo writes FLOW_TYPE itself, after the page's
# handler has hidden the height override again (:98-113). The write is proved by the vehicle's
# echo, and put back.
#
# SITL's copter lists FLOW_TYPE 0 and, with no sensor, none of FLOW_ORIENT_YAW, the scalers or the
# positions: their boxes show, disabled. The numbers' writes and the legacy page's "Enable" are
# covered by the unit tests in crates/mp-gui/src/config/optical_flow.rs.
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760 started from tools/sitl/params/copter.parm. Run as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/config-optflow.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760
#
# A run that stops half way can leave FLOW_TYPE at 1; the first expectation on it then fails until
# a fresh SITL.

screen params
window 1600x1200
budget 7
# A config.xml of its own, so the "Show me again?" boxes this script clicks are not already
# suppressed by the settings of the machine running it.
env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml
# RawParamWarning, on the Full Parameter List's Activate (ConfigRawParams.cs:92): "Show me
# again?" unticked, so no later visit asks, and OK.
# The vehicle first: a click before its first heartbeat is a click the screen may forget
# (vehicle.connected only says the link is open).
expect vehicle.count > 0
click raw-param-warning-again
click raw-param-warning-ok

click param-download
expect params.held > 1000
expect params.value.FLOW_TYPE 0

click tab-setup
expect config.optflow.active false
click setup-page-ConfigOptional
click setup-page-ConfigHWOptFlow
expect setup.page ConfigHWOptFlow
expect config.optflow.active true
expect config.optflow.enabled true
expect config.optflow.heading Optical Flow

# The new-style page.
expect config.optflow.enable.visible false
expect config.optflow.type.visible true
expect config.optflow.type.enabled true
expect config.optflow.type 0
expect config.optflow.type.text None
expect config.optflow.flow_orient_yaw.visible true
expect config.optflow.flow_orient_yaw.enabled false
expect config.optflow.flow_fxscaler.enabled false
expect config.optflow.flow_pos_x.enabled false
# Not a rover: the height override and its labels are hidden.
expect config.optflow.flow_hgt_ovr.visible false
expect config.optflow.height.labels.visible false
expect config.optflow.write none

# The type: PX4Flow, then None again.
click optflow-FLOW_TYPE
click optflow-FLOW_TYPE-1
expect config.optflow.type 1
expect config.optflow.type.text PX4Flow
expect config.optflow.write FLOW_TYPE 1 accepted
expect params.value.FLOW_TYPE 1
expect config.optflow.flow_hgt_ovr.visible false

click optflow-FLOW_TYPE
click optflow-FLOW_TYPE-0
expect config.optflow.type 0
expect config.optflow.write FLOW_TYPE 0 accepted
expect params.value.FLOW_TYPE 0
expect config.optflow.message none
expect config.optflow.writes.pending 0

click setup-page-ConfigOptional
expect config.optflow.active false
